#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9713 expect=violation domain=SV
#note "H2 conditional TV presence rule (minted 2026-08-19; amends the D1 always-present ratification by explicit owner acceptance): subject visits are recorded - SV is present - but the study ships no TV dataset. Sensitivity is Dataset, so the absence is reported ONCE against SV although SV has two rows; the TV-joining consistency rules are gated (Requirements.Variables TV.VISITNUM / the SD1023 guards) and stay silent instead of flooding."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset SV class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVSTDTC  type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Visit"
---
S1 | SV | 001 | 1 | SCREENING | 2020-01-01
S1 | SV | 001 | 2 | WEEK 2    | 2020-01-15
